# Oversight dashboard date range (rule 187)

Extends rule 186. Rule 186 §5 defines every KPI over "the clinic day"; this
rule widens the four PERIOD KPIs from one day to an inclusive range of days.
A one-day range (`start_date == end_date`) is numerically identical to the
rule-186 single-day dashboard. Nothing here changes a KPI formula, a role, a
permission, the branch scope or the read-only posture of rule 186.

## 1. The range

1. Parameters: `start_date`, `end_date`, strict `YYYY-MM-DD`, both **inclusive**
   clinic (Asia/Makassar, WITA) calendar dates read through `ClinicalClock` —
   never UTC `now()`/`today()`, never a browser/device/request timezone.
2. One value object, `App\Modules\ClinicOversight\Support\ClinicalDateRange`,
   built from two strict `ClinicalDayWindow` values so the WITA→UTC conversion
   and the strict `Y-m-d` round-trip parse live in exactly one place:
   - `startUtc` = `start_date 00:00:00 WITA` in UTC (inclusive);
   - `endExclusiveUtc` = **the day after** `end_date` `00:00:00 WITA` in UTC
     (exclusive).
   Example: `2026-10-12..2026-10-30` = UTC `[2026-10-11 16:00:00, 2026-10-30 16:00:00)`.
3. TIMESTAMP columns (`paid_at`, `cancelled_at`) compare as
   `col >= startUtc AND col < endExclusiveUtc`. **Never `23:59:59`** as an end
   workaround, never `whereDate()`, never a function or timezone conversion on
   the column (index-friendly). DATE columns (`visit_date`) compare as
   `[start_date, end_date + 1 day)`.
4. Default (no date parameter): `start_date = end_date =` the clinical today.
   **Reset** returns both dates to today and keeps the selected (authorized)
   branch.

## 2. The one compatibility rule

5. `OversightDashboardFilterRequest` (dashboard only — other oversight surfaces
   keep `OversightFilterRequest`):
   - no `start_date` / `end_date` / `date` → today WITA;
   - `start_date` AND `end_date` → that range;
   - **only one of the two → REJECTED** (never guessed);
   - legacy `date` alone → that single day (old links/bookmarks keep meaning);
     `date` mixed with `start_date`/`end_date` → REJECTED.
6. **A reversed range is REJECTED, never exchanged.**
7. Bounds: dates within `2000-01-01..2099-12-31` (keeps every bound literal a
   valid four-digit-year PostgreSQL timestamp — year 0 / five-digit years would
   be a 500); span at most **`ClinicalDateRange::MAX_DAYS` = 366 inclusive days**
   (a full year incl. a leap day — the resource bound). The value object
   enforces the same limits defensively; `dateRange()` FAILS CLOSED (validation
   error) rather than falling back to today for a request that asked for
   something else.
7a. The dashboard request validates ONLY `branch_id` and the date keys. The
    parent's list-page keys (`visit_date_from/to`, `status`, `search`, …) are
    deliberately NOT inherited: the dashboard ignores them, an unvalidated key
    never reaches `filters()`, and the parent's field-reference rule would
    otherwise make `visit_date_from[]=…` a 500 on this surface too.
8. Order and span are checked in `withValidator()` once both dates are valid
   strings — **never with the field-reference rule `after_or_equal:start_date`**,
   which hands the OTHER field's raw value to `DateTime` and turns
   `start_date[]=…` into a TypeError (HTTP 500).
9. A refused filter on the page redirects to the dashboard itself (never
   `url()->previous()`, which could be the same invalid URL and loop), carrying
   only a shape-valid `branch_id`; the JSON feed answers 422. Route permission
   middleware runs BEFORE validation, so a caller without access gets 403, never
   a 422 that answers for the dates.

## 3. KPIs over the range (formulas are rule 186 §5, unchanged)

10. **Jumlah Pasien** — DISTINCT `patient_id` over the whole range (a patient
    who came three times is one); checked-in, not cancelled, not soft-deleted.
    The all-branch total is distinct PEOPLE across branches AND dates — never
    the sum of the branch rows (payload carries both).
11. **Jumlah Transaksi** — DISTINCT cashier batches (`payment_batch_uuid`,
    NULL → `'payment:'||id`) with `paid_at` in the range; a carry-over batch
    that also settles an old receivable is still one transaction. Per invoice
    branch; once overall.
12. **Jumlah Omzet** — `SUM(trx_rme_payments.amount)` by `paid_at` in the range,
    invoice-branch attribution; an old visit's invoice paid inside the range
    counts in the range. Never lab `trx_payments`.
13. **PIUTANG AKTIF PER SAAT INI** — **NOT a period KPI.** The current
    outstanding balance, identical for every range. The repository method takes
    **no range parameter at all**, so no caller can date-filter it; the payload
    states `receivable_basis = current_balance`; the page, print and CSV label it
    "saldo saat ini, tidak mengikuti periode tanggal".
14. **Jumlah Pasien Cancel** — `cancelled_at` in the range; never `updated_at`,
    never `visit_date`; a no-show is not a cancellation.

## 4. Payload, refresh, export

15. `METRIC_VERSION = 2`: payload carries `start_date`, `end_date`,
    `day_count`, `is_single_day`, `is_today` (single day that is today),
    `includes_today`, `receivable_basis` — the single `date` key is gone. Bump
    the version again on any future contract change.
16. Auto-refresh (60 s, paused while the tab is hidden, re-authorized every
    call) uses the page's OWN filter (`start_date`, `end_date`, legacy `date`,
    `branch_id` only — anything else on the URL is dropped). An explicit range
    stays pinned across refreshes; the default (no dates) keeps following the
    clinical today. Only the newest request may write the cards
    (`requestSeq` guard) — an older response resolving late is discarded.
    When the default view rolls over at WITA midnight, the component announces
    the moved range (`oversight-range-moved`) so the pickers follow and
    "Terapkan Filter" can never silently pin yesterday; an explicit range never
    moves, so a user's unsubmitted edit is never overwritten.
17. CSV and print use the same request rule and range: every CSV row carries
    `Tanggal Mulai (WITA)` / `Tanggal Akhir (WITA)`; file name
    `dashboard-finance-data-analyst-{start}_sd_{end}.csv` (a one-day range keeps
    the original `…-{date}.csv`); print states the period and day count and its
    back link keeps the range. Audit metadata uses the existing allowlisted keys
    `date_from` / `date_to` (no allowlist widening).

## 5. Unchanged (do not "fix" here)

18. Branch: `branch_id` only NARROWS the server-resolved `ClinicOversightScope`
    set; a date range never widens authorization; a forged branch yields empty.
19. RBAC: `view_finance_analytics_dashboard` (+ `export_oversight_data` for
    CSV/print) — Finance Klinik and Data Analyst; the lab `Finance` role and all
    operational roles stay denied. No permission, role or migration added.
20. Read-only: every statement is a SELECT; no cache; no write path.
21. Performance: one grouped aggregation per KPI, query count independent of
    branch count AND range length; existing indexes
    (`trx_clinic_visits(branch_id, visit_date, status)`,
    `trx_rme_payments(branch_id, paid_at)`) — no index added for this revision.

## 6. Regression requirements

22. `tests/Feature/ClinicOversight/ClinicOversightDashboardDateRangeTest.php`
    (mandatory critical-gate suite) pins every clause above, including the WITA
    midnight boundaries on both ends, end-date inclusivity, cross-branch and
    cross-date patient dedup, carry-over batches, the current-balance Piutang,
    the compatibility rule, the 366-day bound, refresh/reset/export/print
    consistency and RBAC. `ClinicOversightDashboardKpiTest.php` is the
    single-day regression and must keep passing unchanged except for the
    service signature (a date `D` is the range `D..D`).
